ioned at 100 : 60 by weight and mixed whole until the liquid runs clear. Once injected it penetrates deep into a crack and cures to a shrink-free solid mass that bonds the two faces back together.\n\n## What it\'s for\n\nStructural crack repair. It is used to seal and permanently bond cracks in concrete floors, walls, slabs, water tanks and sea walls, and to fill honeycombing and cavities in concrete and masonry. Because it is shrink free, waterproof and stronger than the parent concrete, it is specified on heavy structures — bridges, dams and buildings — as well as on ordinary building repairs.\n\n## Key specifications\n\nCompressive strength exceeds 40 MPa at one day and 70 MPa at seven days to BS 6319 Part 2; flexural strength exceeds 30 MPa and tensile strength 15 MPa at seven days. Specific gravity is 1.02 to 1.08 and fresh mix density 1.02 kg/L. Brookfield viscosity is 2 to 6 poise at 30 °C — about 400 mPa·s — which is what lets it travel into a hairline crack. Pot life is 80 to 150 minutes at 30 °C and 65 % RH against a specification minimum of 50, and initial set is under 24 hours. Water permeability is capped at 2 % to ASTM C 881, and bond strength to ASTM D 4541 fails in the concrete rather than the bond line. Shelf life is 24 months. No BIS mark is declared.\n\n## Application notes\n\nThe surface must be strong, dry and free of dust, oil, grease and curing compounds; blast, water-jet, acid-etch (washed to neutral) or grind it, then blow the crack clean with oil-free air. Drill into the crack at 40 to 50 degrees to at least a third of the member depth, fit packers 150 to 500 mm apart, and seal the surface between them with a 30-40 mm wide, 2-3 mm thick band, cured at least 8 hours at 35 °C. Inject with closed-container equipment at a minimum of 2 bar until resin emerges from the next packer, then leave undisturbed 24 hours. Mix only what the pot life allows, mix the whole pack, and never thin it with solvent.\n\n## What\'s in the box\n\nOne 3 kg pack: base resin and hardener, pre-proportioned 100 : 60 by weight. Also supplied in 1 kg.','[{\"key\": \"epoxy_type\", \"unit\": null, \"label\": \"Epoxy system type\", \"value\": \"Injection resin\"}, {\"key\": \"compressive_strength_mpa\", \"unit\": \"MPa\", \"label\": \"Compressive strength\", \"value\": \"70 MPa\"}, {\"key\": \"bond_strength_concrete_mpa\", \"unit\": \"MPa\", \"label\": \"Bond strength to concrete\", \"value\": \"12 MPa\"}, {\"key\": \"pot_life_min\", \"unit\": \"min\", \"label\": \"Pot life at 30 °C\", \"value\": \"80 min\"}, {\"key\": \"full_cure_time_days\", \"unit\": \"days\", \"label\": \"Full cure time\", \"value\": \"7 days\"}, {\"key\": \"coverage\", \"unit\": null, \"label\": \"Coverage / yield\", \"value\": \"Fills the crack volume injected — a 3 kg pack yields about 2.9 litres of grout at a fresh-mix density of 1.02 kg/L\"}, {\"key\": \"pack_size_kg\", \"unit\": \"kg\", \"label\": \"Kit / pack size\", \"value\": \"3 kg\"}, {\"key\": \"application_thickness_mm\", \"unit\": null, \"label\": \"Application thickness per layer\", \"value\": \"Injected into structural cracks and honeycombs at a minimum pressure of 0.2 N/mm² (2 bar); nozzles set 150–500 mm apart depending on crack width, depth and water pressure\"}]','{\"total\": 49, \"filled\": 49, \"groups\": [{\"key\": \"product_identity\", \"rows\": [{\"key\": \"epoxy_type\", \"unit\": null, \"label\": \"Epoxy system type\", \"value\": \"Injection resin\", \"compare\": true, \"data_type\": \"enum\", \"confidence\": null, \"provenance\": \"fetched\", \"source_url\": null}, {\"key\": \"application_form\", \"unit\": null, \"label\": \"Consistency / form\", \"value\": \"Low-viscosity injection liquid\", \"compare\": true, \"data_type\": \"enum\", \"confidence\": null, \"provenance\": \"fetched\", \"source_url\": null}, {\"key\": \"model_number\", \"unit\": null, \"label\": \"Model / product code\", \"value\": \"206\", \"compare\": false, \"data_type\": \"text\", \"confidence\": null, \"provenance\": 