", \"light_to_solar_gain\", \"solar_heat_gain_coefficient\", \"u_value_w_m2k\", \"sound_reduction_db\", \"impact_safety_class\", \"nominal_thickness_mm\", \"max_pane_width_mm\"], \"meta_description\": \"AIS Ecosense Edge Natura Plus 6 mm solar-control low-E glass for single glazing: VLT 45%, SHGC 0.42, U 4.6 W/m²K. Per sqft, cut to size, AP & Telangana.\"}','skus/e0/GLS-AIS-EDGE-NATURAPLUS/img/1-card.webp','LNBgiHRNV;WAkvV?ROV?R=W9Riad',4.3,'https://www.aisglass.com/building-and-construction/coated-for-exteriors/ais-ecosense/','{\"total\": 47, \"filled\": 47, \"images\": 5, \"brochures\": 0, \"computed_at\": \"2026-08-25T09:18:51.314Z\", \"placeholders\": 0, \"by_provenance\": {\"derived\": 2, \"fetched\": 11, \"verified\": 0, \"ai_filled\": 34}}','2026-08-23 00:04:03','2026-08-25 09:18:51',6,NULL),(50,50,'GLS-GUA-CLIMAGUARD-BLUE5','5 mm, Blue, monolithic single pane',70.00,70.00,'fetched','https://www.indiamart.com/proddetail/coated-glass-climaguard-2850058948697.html','IndiaMART dealer listing (Goutam Glass Incorporation, Hyderabad) for \'Coated Glass ClimaGuard\' at ₹70/sq ft; the listing covers 4–12 mm and all shades, so the 5 mm Blue rate should be re-quoted from a Guardian dealer.','2026-08-23 00:00:00',18.00,1,'sqft',1.000,'in_stock','Guardian ClimaGuard Blue 5 mm durable coated solar-control glass for homes. Clear float substrate, max size 3660 × 2550 mm, coating on surface 2. Sold per sqft.','## What it is\n\nGuardian ClimaGuard Blue is a 5 mm durable coated solar-control glass from Guardian\'s ClimaGuard residential range, made on a clear float substrate and supplied as a single annealed monolithic pane. Guardian lists the coating as usable monolithic or in an insulating glass unit, with heat-strengthened, heat-soaked, laminated and bent processing options and no edge deletion required. As delivered it is not a safety glass; a processor can toughen or laminate it to IS 2553 Part 1. It weighs about 12.5 kg per square metre, so a 1200 × 1800 mm pane is roughly 27 kg.\n\n## What it\'s for\n\nWindows and residential glazing — Guardian names windows, skylights, roof windows and doors for this product — in houses, apartments and small commercial buildings across Andhra Pradesh and Telangana. It is suitable for exterior use with the coating on surface 2, and it is rated for overhead glazing, where it should be laminated or toughened to satisfy IS 2553 Part 1.\n\n## Key specifications\n\nGuardian publishes the thickness range (3.5, 4 and 5 mm), a maximum pane size under 3660 × 2550 mm and the blue appearance, but not optical or thermal numbers for India, so the following are indicative values for a 5 mm durable-coated blue solar-control glass: visible light transmission about 36%, external reflection about 18%, solar heat gain coefficient about 0.45, U-value about 5.7 W/m²K, emissivity about 0.84, UV transmission about 20% and sound reduction about 30 dB. Thermal-shock resistance is 40 °C and bending strength 41 MPa, as for annealed float. The substrate is IS 14900 float glass; IS 16231 applies only if the pane is made into a DGU.\n\n## Installation notes\n\nGlaze with the coated face towards the interior (surface 2), with at least 12 mm edge engagement, setting blocks and neutral-cure silicone or EPDM gaskets in uPVC or aluminium frames. The annealed coated pane is cuttable and needs no edge deletion. Handle the coated side with clean gloves, avoid abrasive cleaning on it, and wash with water and a mild detergent. Order toughened or laminated panes for doors, skylights and large openings.\n\n## What\'s supplied\n\nCut-to-size panes with as-cut edges and the coated face marked, interleaved with paper or cork pads and delivered on an A-frame or in a wooden crate from dealer stock. Minimum order 10 sqft; 4 and 5 mm are on Guardian\'s short lead time, typically about 7 days through Hyderabad dealers. Warranty is recorded as 120 months on the coating, to be confirmed with the dealer. HSN 7005, GST 18%.','[{\"key\": \"visible_lig